115 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 63 0 R
/T (Another major limitation of existing commercial monitoring systems is their dependency on a continuous electrical grid or the frequent replacement of non-rechargeable batteries. In many rural, off-grid, or offshore aquaculture environments, accessing a stable power infrastructure is either technically impractical or economically prohibitive. Systems relying solely on standard batteries require constant manual maintenance, which increases labor costs and defeats the primary purpose of an automated monitoring system. Therefore, for a monitoring system to be truly effective and scalable in these remote locations, it must be highly energy-efficient and self-sustaining.)
/E (Another major limitation of existing commercial monitoring systems is their dependency on a continuous electrical grid or the frequent replacement of non-rechargeable batteries. In many rural, off-grid, or offshore aquaculture environments, accessing a stable power infrastructure is either technically impractical or economically prohibitive. Systems relying solely on standard batteries require constant manual maintenance, which increases labor costs and defeats the primary purpose of an automated monitoring system. Therefore, for a monitoring system to be truly effective and scalable in these remote locations, it must be highly energy-efficient and self-sustaining.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
116 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 63 0 R
/T (Furthermore, isolated measurement tools fail to provide historical data tracking and remote accessibility. Farm managers require the ability to monitor their facilities from any location and receive immediate alerts when water parameters reach critical thresholds. Without proper cloud integration, data remains localized, preventing comprehensive analysis and proactive decision-making.)
/E (Furthermore, isolated measurement tools fail to provide historical data tracking and remote accessibility. Farm managers require the ability to monitor their facilities from any location and receive immediate alerts when water parameters reach critical thresholds. Without proper cloud integration, data remains localized, preventing comprehensive analysis and proactive decision-making.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
