122 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 64 0 R
/T (The scope of this internship project covers the end-to-end development of an autonomous IoT hardware node, beginning with component selection and circuit design, and concluding with cloud integration and field evaluation. The project was designed as a modular embedded system that demonstrates how renewable energy and IoT technologies can be combined to create a reliable, scalable monitoring solution for aquaculture.)
/E (The scope of this internship project covers the end-to-end development of an autonomous IoT hardware node, beginning with component selection and circuit design, and concluding with cloud integration and field evaluation. The project was designed as a modular embedded system that demonstrates how renewable energy and IoT technologies can be combined to create a reliable, scalable monitoring solution for aquaculture.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 64 0 R
/T (The first phase focused on hardware architecture and power management. A custom PCB docking board was utilized to house an ESP32 microcontroller, integrated with a solar charge controller and an MT3608 boost converter. This power management layer was specifically designed to harvest energy from a solar panel to sustain a 4-cell battery pack, ensuring continuous off-grid operation.)
/E (The first phase focused on hardware architecture and power management. A custom PCB docking board was utilized to house an ESP32 microcontroller, integrated with a solar charge controller and an MT3608 boost converter. This power management layer was specifically designed to harvest energy from a solar panel to sustain a 4-cell battery pack, ensuring continuous off-grid operation.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
124 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 64 0 R
/T (The second phase involved sensor integration and data acquisition. A commercial analog turbidity sensor and a waterproof metal-tipped temperature probe were interfaced with the microcontroller. Proper voltage divider networks and Analog-to-Digital Converter \(ADC\) mapping techniques were implemented to accurately read environmental parameters and safely track the real-time battery voltage.)
/E (The second phase involved sensor integration and data acquisition. A commercial analog turbidity sensor and a waterproof metal-tipped temperature probe were interfaced with the microcontroller. Proper voltage divider networks and Analog-to-Digital Converter \(ADC\) mapping techniques were implemented to accurately read environmental parameters and safely track the real-time battery voltage.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
125 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 64 0 R
/T (Cloud integration and software development constituted another significant component of the project. The ESP32 was programmed to periodically sample sensor data and transmit it over a local Wi-Fi network. The backend integration was established using the Thinger.io platform, where a graphical dashboard was developed to visualize real-time water temperature, turbidity levels, and system battery status. Additionally, the architecture incorporated Sinric Pro to bridge the system with smart home ecosystems, enabling voice-controlled queries via Amazon Alexa.)
/E (Cloud integration and software development constituted another significant component of the project. The ESP32 was programmed to periodically sample sensor data and transmit it over a local Wi-Fi network. The backend integration was established using the Thinger.io platform, where a graphical dashboard was developed to visualize real-time water temperature, turbidity levels, and system battery status. Additionally, the architecture incorporated Sinric Pro to bridge the system with smart home ecosystems, enabling voice-controlled queries via Amazon Alexa.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
126 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 64 0 R
/T (Finally, practical field testing was conducted to validate the functionality, energy efficiency, and reliability of the complete system. The hardware was exposed to variable weather conditions over a one-week period, during which battery voltage levels were manually tracked using a digital multimeter. The system's power harvesting capability in cloudy conditions, sensor data accuracy, and stable cloud communication were rigorously evaluated to ensure stable performance.)
/E (Finally, practical field testing was conducted to validate the functionality, energy efficiency, and reliability of the complete system. The hardware was exposed to variable weather conditions over a one-week period, during which battery voltage levels were manually tracked using a digital multimeter. The system's power harvesting capability in cloudy conditions, sensor data accuracy, and stable cloud communication were rigorously evaluated to ensure stable performance.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 64 0 R
/T (Overall, the project demonstrates the successful integration of embedded hardware, renewable energy management, and modern IoT cloud platforms into a practical, self-sustaining solution capable of addressing real-world challenges faced by contemporary aquaculture facilities.)
/E (Overall, the project demonstrates the successful integration of embedded hardware, renewable energy management, and modern IoT cloud platforms into a practical, self-sustaining solution capable of addressing real-world challenges faced by contemporary aquaculture facilities.)
/Pg 14 0 R
