/E (4.1 Embedded Software and Sensor Calibration)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
163 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 67 0 R
/T (The software architecture of the ESP32 node was developed using the Arduino Integrated Development Environment \(IDE\). The core logic was written in C/C++, and iterative testing was conducted directly on the ESP32 hardware to ensure stable data acquisition and processing. The microcontroller was programmed to periodically sample analog data from the turbidity sensor and the battery voltage divider network. For water temperature acquisition, the system utilizes a digital communication protocol to interface with the metal-tipped probe, ensuring high-precision readings. Once the raw sensor data is acquired, the ESP32 processes these values locally, applying calibration algorithms to convert analog ADC \(Analog-to-Digital Converter\) readings into meaningful metrics, such as actual voltage levels and turbidity percentages. To maintain system stability, the software includes timing routines that manage the frequency of sensor sampling and prevent network congestion during Wi-Fi data transmissions.)
/E (The software architecture of the ESP32 node was developed using the Arduino Integrated Development Environment \(IDE\). The core logic was written in C/C++, and iterative testing was conducted directly on the ESP32 hardware to ensure stable data acquisition and processing. The microcontroller was programmed to periodically sample analog data from the turbidity sensor and the battery voltage divider network. For water temperature acquisition, the system utilizes a digital communication protocol to interface with the metal-tipped probe, ensuring high-precision readings. Once the raw sensor data is acquired, the ESP32 processes these values locally, applying calibration algorithms to convert analog ADC \(Analog-to-Digital Converter\) readings into meaningful metrics, such as actual voltage levels and turbidity percentages. To maintain system stability, the software includes timing routines that manage the frequency of sensor sampling and prevent network congestion during Wi-Fi data transmissions.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
