176 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 68 0 R
/T (The primary objective of this internship project was successfully achieved through the design, implementation, and testing of an autonomous, solar-powered IoT system for real-time water quality monitoring. By integrating an ESP32 microcontroller with precise environmental sensors and a robust power management circuit, the project demonstrated a practical and scalable solution for continuous monitoring in aquaculture facilities. The hardware architecture proved its reliability and energy efficiency during field testing. The custom power management system successfully sustained the operation of the remote node and charged the battery pack even under predominantly cloudy weather conditions. This validated the system's capability for off-grid operation, significantly reducing the need for manual maintenance and reliance on conventional power grids. Furthermore, the embedded software, developed using the Arduino IDE, established seamless cloud communication. The integration with Thinger.io provided a user-friendly dashboard for real-time data visualization, while the implementation of Sinric Pro introduced modern, voice-controlled accessibility via Amazon Alexa. Overall, this project provided comprehensive practical experience in embedded systems, hardware design, power electronics, and modern IoT cloud platforms. The developed prototype stands as a highly effective tool that addresses real-world logistical challenges in modern agriculture, ensuring optimal water conditions through continuous, automated, and self-sustaining environmental monitoring.)
/E (The primary objective of this internship project was successfully achieved through the design, implementation, and testing of an autonomous, solar-powered IoT system for real-time water quality monitoring. By integrating an ESP32 microcontroller with precise environmental sensors and a robust power management circuit, the project demonstrated a practical and scalable solution for continuous monitoring in aquaculture facilities. The hardware architecture proved its reliability and energy efficiency during field testing. The custom power management system successfully sustained the operation of the remote node and charged the battery pack even under predominantly cloudy weather conditions. This validated the system's capability for off-grid operation, significantly reducing the need for manual maintenance and reliance on conventional power grids. Furthermore, the embedded software, developed using the Arduino IDE, established seamless cloud communication. The integration with Thinger.io provided a user-friendly dashboard for real-time data visualization, while the implementation of Sinric Pro introduced modern, voice-controlled accessibility via Amazon Alexa. Overall, this project provided comprehensive practical experience in embedded systems, hardware design, power electronics, and modern IoT cloud platforms. The developed prototype stands as a highly effective tool that addresses real-world logistical challenges in modern agriculture, ensuring optimal water conditions through continuous, automated, and self-sustaining environmental monitoring.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
