/Title (At the beginning of the observation period, the initial battery voltage was measured at 3.08V. Over the course of approximately one week, the system was exposed to predominantly cloudy weather conditions, including a brief period of rain. Despite the lack of direct and strong sunlight, the solar panel and power management circuit successfully harvested enough energy to charge the 4-cell battery pack. By the end of the observation period, the multimeter readings indicated a voltage increase to approximately 3.60V.)
