/Title (The developed system follows a modular hardware architecture to ensure autonomy, reliability, and efficient power management in remote aquaculture environments. The architecture is divided into three main layers: the Power Management Layer, the Data Acquisition Layer, and the Processing & Communication Layer. Each layer performs specific tasks while interacting with the others through custom-designed PCB routing. The Power Management Layer is responsible for sustaining the autonomous operation of the node. It consists of a 4-cell battery pack that is continuously recharged by a solar panel. An onboard solar charge controller, coupled with an MT3608 boost converter module, regulates the incoming solar energy to safely charge the batteries and provide a stable operating voltage. The Data Acquisition Layer interacts directly with the physical environment. It incorporates a waterproof metal-tipped probe for temperature measurement and a commercially available analog turbidity sensor. Additionally, a voltage divider network is integrated to safely step down and read the battery voltage levels. The Processing & Communication Layer acts as the core of the system. An ESP32 microcontroller processes the analog and digital signals from the sensors, applies necessary calibration factors, and manages the Wi-Fi communication. It ensures that the acquired data is reliably transmitted to the cloud interfaces. This layered architecture separates hardware responsibilities, making the system easier to maintain, test, and deploy.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 513 0 R
>>
endobj
551 0 obj
<<
/Title (Several modern electronic components and IoT frameworks were used during the development of the project to ensure high performance and reliability. ESP32 Microcontroller was selected as the primary processing unit due to its integrated Wi-Fi capabilities, robust processing power, and efficient power management suitable for IoT applications. Custom PCB Docking Board was utilized to securely mount the ESP32 and integrate the voltage divider network, ensuring reliable pin connections and overall system modularity. MT3608 Boost Converter & Solar Controller served as the core of the power management system. These modules safely regulate solar energy input and step up the voltage to power the microcontroller consistently, even under predominantly cloudy weather conditions. Environmental Sensors included a digital waterproof metal-tipped temperature probe and an analog turbidity sensor to accurately capture real-time water quality metrics without the risk of corrosion. Thinger.io was utilized as the primary IoT cloud platform. It enabled the rapid creation of an interactive web dashboard for real-time visualization of sensor data and battery status. Sinric Pro was integrated to bridge the ESP32 hardware with smart home ecosystems, enabling voice-controlled interactions and status queries via Amazon Alexa.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 514 0 R
>>
endobj
