565 0 obj
<<
/Title (To overcome these combined biological, logistical, and infrastructural challenges, this project introduces an autonomous, solar-powered IoT solution. By integrating efficient solar energy harvesting with low-power microcontrollers and wireless data transmission, the system continuously tracks water quality and relays data to a centralized cloud dashboard, completely eliminating the need for daily manual intervention and dedicated power grid connections.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 559 0 R
/Prev 572 0 R
>>
endobj
566 0 obj
<<
/Title (The first phase focused on hardware architecture and power management. A custom PCB docking board was utilized to house an ESP32 microcontroller, integrated with a solar charge controller and an MT3608 boost converter. This power management layer was specifically designed to harvest energy from a solar panel to sustain a 4-cell battery pack, ensuring continuous off-grid operation.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 547 0 R
/Prev 560 0 R
/Next 573 0 R
>>
endobj
567 0 obj
<<
/Title (Finally, practical field testing was conducted to validate the functionality, energy efficiency, and reliability of the complete system. The hardware was exposed to variable weather conditions over a one-week period, during which battery voltage levels were manually tracked using a digital multimeter. The system's power harvesting capability in cloudy conditions, sensor data accuracy, and stable cloud communication were rigorously evaluated to ensure stable performance.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 547 0 R
/Prev 574 0 R
/Next 561 0 R
>>
endobj
