570 0 obj
<<
/Title (The rapid growth of the aquaculture industry requires continuous and precise monitoring of water parameters to ensure aquatic health and maximize yield. Traditional manual sampling methods are time-consuming, labor-intensive, and fail to provide real-time insights. As environmental and operational demands increase, there is a critical need for autonomous systems capable of continuous data acquisition and remote monitoring.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 564 0 R
/Next 576 0 R
>>
endobj
571 0 obj
<<
/Title (Besides technical implementation, the internship provided an opportunity to gain practical experience in modern electronics and IoT methodologies. The completed system consists of an ESP32 microcontroller, an analog turbidity sensor, a temperature probe, a custom power management circuit \(including an MT3608 boost converter\), and a web-based dashboard on Thinger.io. Together, these components create a reliable, low-power architecture capable of real-time environmental monitoring.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 564 0 R
/Prev 577 0 R
>>
endobj
572 0 obj
<<
/Title (1.2 Problem Statement)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 559 0 R
/Prev 564 0 R
/First 578 0 R
/Last 579 0 R
/Count -3
/Next 565 0 R
>>
endobj
573 0 obj
<<
/Title (The second phase involved sensor integration and data acquisition. A commercial analog turbidity sensor and a waterproof metal-tipped temperature probe were interfaced with the microcontroller. Proper voltage divider networks and Analog-to-Digital Converter \(ADC\) mapping techniques were implemented to accurately read environmental parameters and safely track the real-time battery voltage.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 547 0 R
/Prev 566 0 R
/Next 574 0 R
>>
endobj
574 0 obj
<<
/Title (Cloud integration and software development constituted another significant component of the project. The ESP32 was programmed to periodically sample sensor data and transmit it over a local Wi-Fi network. The backend integration was established using the Thinger.io platform, where a graphical dashboard was developed to visualize real-time water temperature, turbidity levels, and system battery status. Additionally, the architecture incorporated Sinric Pro to bridge the system with smart home ecosystems, enabling voice-controlled queries via Amazon Alexa.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 547 0 R
/Prev 573 0 R
/Next 567 0 R
>>
endobj
575 0 obj
<<
/Title (SOFTWARE DESIGN AND CLOUD INTEGRATION)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 546 0 R
/Prev 568 0 R
/Next 569 0 R
>>
endobj
576 0 obj
<<
/Title (The primary objective of this internship project was to design and implement a solar-powered Internet of Things \(IoT\) node for real-time water quality monitoring. Instead of relying on conventional grid power, the proposed system operates autonomously using a solar panel and a battery management circuit, ensuring continuous operation even in remote environments.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 564 0 R
/Prev 570 0 R
/Next 577 0 R
>>
endobj
577 0 obj
<<
/Title (The project also aimed to demonstrate how embedded systems and cloud technologies can be combined to solve real-world agricultural problems. Throughout the internship, the system was developed by following engineering principles such as hardware integration, power management design, microcontroller programming, and cloud platform configuration.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 564 0 R
/Prev 576 0 R
/Next 571 0 R
>>
endobj
578 0 obj
<<
/Title <>
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 572 0 R
/Next 580 0 R
>>
endobj
579 0 obj
<<
/Title (Furthermore, isolated measurement tools fail to provide historical data tracking and remote accessibility. Farm managers require the ability to monitor their facilities from any location and receive immediate alerts when water parameters reach critical thresholds. Without proper cloud integration, data remains localized, preventing comprehensive analysis and proactive decision-making.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 572 0 R
/Prev 580 0 R
>>
endobj
580 0 obj
<<
/Title (Another major limitation of existing commercial monitoring systems is their dependency on a continuous electrical grid or the frequent replacement of non-rechargeable batteries. In many rural, off-grid, or offshore aquaculture environments, accessing a stable power infrastructure is either technically impractical or economically prohibitive. Systems relying solely on standard batteries require constant manual maintenance, which increases labor costs and defeats the primary purpose of an automated monitoring system. Therefore, for a monitoring system to be truly effective and scalable in these remote locations, it must be highly energy-efficient and self-sustaining.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 572 0 R
/Prev 578 0 R
/Next 579 0 R
>>
endobj
